      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That error code 1004 is the classic \"Excel is having a moment\" panic, and it's often because the destination cell is already occupied by a stubborn, unmovable object or a misbehaving macro object sheet. It's like trying to shove a giant, invisible brick into a tiny hole; the macro just gets confused and throws up its hands.\n\nSince you mentioned the names seem fine, you might want to check if there are any hidden \"goblin\" objects lurking in the workbook that are blocking the path. Sometimes, just adding a little bit of cleanup code to remove any existing objects in the destination range before you try to copy the data can solve the problem.\n\nHere is a revised version of your macro that includes a small \"sanity check\" to clear out any potential obstacles before the copy operation happens. This should help the macro navigate the glitchy waters more smoothly.\n\n```vba\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim wsSource As Worksheet\n    Dim wsDest As Worksheet\n    Dim rng As Range\n    \n    Set wsSource = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Data_Input\")\n    Set wsDest = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Recon_Report\")\n    \n    ' Clear any existing objects",
